special_abilities:
  - name: "Full Bionic Conversion"
    description: "Every ninja ''borg is a full conversion cyborg built to the maximum strength and prowess: 280 M.D.C., bionic P.S. 30, P.P. 24 and Spd 176 (120 mph), all stored. Only the face, the brain and a few organs remain human. Simulated sense of touch is only 43%, and Prowl suffers -40% unless the Sound Suppression System is working. The book prints no M.D.C. by location for this body. Most are built to look as humanoid as possible; hidden under a trench coat, cloak, robe, hat and dark glasses the ''borg passes casual contact only, with a 5% chance per ten minutes of being recognized as a ''borg on a busy street."
  - name: "Sound Suppression System"
    description: "An emitter built alongside the skin cancels the noise the body makes with sound waves of the opposite frequency, helped by rubber soles and joints. Together they eliminate the -40% Prowl penalty, but only while the ''borg moves or climbs slowly (Spd 10 at most) and wears light M.D.C. armor; heavy cyborg armor muffles the emitter, and any sudden movement brings the full penalty back."
  - name: "Standard Bionic Accessories"
    description: "Built into every ninja ''borg: one or two multi-optic eyes, amplified hearing, a motion detector, a bionic lung, a climb cord, a garrote wrist wire, a concealed laser rod (1D6 M.D.), retractable vibro-blades (2D6 M.D.), and a concealed particle beam in the torso (6D6+6 M.D., range 1000 feet/305 m) behind a sliding chest plate; armor can be built to slide aside with the panel."
  - name: "Optional Bionic Accessories"
    description: "About 30% of ninja ''borgs have one or more of: a modulating voice synthesizer, a chemical spray, an additional arm, an additional tail appendage, or the Bionic Fire-breath System. Extra limbs, a tail and the fire-breath are fitted only to a character psychologically able to accept such inhuman changes; the GM decides."
  - name: "Bionic Fire-breath System"
    description: "An optional accessory: a plasma discharger built into the mouth and powered by an easily replaced E-clip in a body compartment, 1D4x10 M.D., range 500 feet (152 m). The lower mouth is replaced by metal and the voice box heavily armored, so the voice becomes an eerie, inhuman bass with a Horror Factor of 9. Only for a ''borg fitted with it."
  - name: "Additional Cybernetics"
    description: "Besides the bionic systems above, 1D4 cybernetic systems of choice, plus the clan''s tracer chip (in the equipment)."
trackable_resources: []
restrictions:
