  - "A clan operative: living expenses are met by the clan, which may add money for a mission, and the tracer chip lets it keep tabs on the character."
extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 8: Japan printed 88-89 (cache p089-p090, text layer, page_offset +1). The entry opens under Ninja ''Borg in the second column of printed 88 (lore and Bionic Conversion & Accessories items 1-2), and item 2 continues onto printed 89, which holds items 3-5 and the O.C.C. block through Cybernetics; the Ninja Techno-Wizard follows. Printed 89 read off a 150 dpi render: every skill bonus and both money figures (1D6x1000, the text layer ciphers the first as !D6xlOOO) agree. || XP: the Ninja Borg, Ninja Crazy, Ninja Jucier column on the Experience Point Tables page (cache p217, printed folio 216), third column, lower block, read off a render: 0 / 2,141 / 4,281 / 8,561 / 17,521 / 25,521 / 35,521 / 50,521 / 71,001 / 96,101 / 131,201 / 181,301 / 231,401 / 281,501 / 341,601. || GROUP: the book files it under the Republic of Japan''s Character Classes (contents, printed 5) with no group heading; stored as men-of-arms (a combat cyborg), following plains-borg. mdc_base is stated, so no men_of_arms line. || BODY AND ATTRIBUTES: 280 M.D.C. as mdc_base; P.S. 30, P.P. 24 and Spd 176 as fixed attribute_dice, the plains-borg and destroyer-borg precedent. The book prints 120 mph as 182 kph (printed 96 has 192 for the same speed); the kph is not stored. No M.D.C. by location is printed, and the class does not use the Japanese Bionic Conversion table on printed 96 (heavy full conversion there is 180 M.D.C.); the class''s own 280 is stored. Mental attributes and P.B. are the character''s own. Not supersedes_race. || SKILLS: catalog base plus printed bonus: Mathematics: Basic 45+10, Radio: Basic 45+15, Radio: Scramblers 35+10, Literacy: Japanese as Literacy: Native Language 40+15, Computer Operation 40+5, Climbing 40+10, Prowl 25+10, Detect Ambush 30+10, Track as Tracking (people) 25+10. Language: Japanese (+20%) as Language: Native Tongue at 98. W.P. four of choice. Hand to Hand: Assassin with no upgrade or price printed, so no hand_to_hand block. The -40% bionic Prowl penalty is conditional and is prose. || RELATED: six, at least one from Rogue (minimums), plus one at levels 4, 8 and 12. Communications +5, Espionage +10, Military +10, Pilot Related +5, Rogue +6, Wilderness +5; Electrical Basic Electronics only; Mechanical basic and automotive only; Medical first aid and criminal sciences and forensics only, stored as First Aid and Forensics (no criminal science row); Domestic, Physical, Pilot, Science, Technical and W.P. any. SECONDARY: six from the same list without the bonuses. || BIONICS: the full conversion, sound suppression, standard and optional accessories and the fire-breath system are abilities, following plains-borg. The RUE bionic systems named (multi-optic eye, bionic lung, climb cord, garrote wrist wire, laser rod) have no catalog rows and are not stubbed; the tracer chip is this book''s tracer-chip row, in the equipment. The optional accessories are a 30% chance and a GM''s call, so they are prose, not a choice. The fire-breath''s Horror Factor 9 applies only to a ''borg fitted with it, so it is not stored. || EQUIPMENT: NF-100 Infiltrator is the IA-100 Infiltrator Body Armor row (printed 184; the class text misprints the prefix). The energy weapon, vibro-blade and ancient weapon are choices from this book''s catalog rows; the four E-clips are a pistol-or-rifle E-clip choice. The micro-film camera and small crowbar are this book''s micro-film-camera and small-crowbar rows (printed 83). The 50 feet of knotted rope is the climbing-rope-per-foot row at 50. || MONEY: 1D6x1000 credits; the 1D6x1000 credits'' worth of black market salable items is not coin and is prose. || CYBERNETICS: 1D4 cybernetic systems of choice plus the tracer chip; the app has no implant pick, so the 1D4 is an ability."
