## Lore

Ninja ''borgs are the deadliest assassins of the tech-ninja clans. They can
absorb as much damage as a soldier in power armor, carry a lethal array of
implanted weapons, and are fitted with special stealth and surveillance
bionics developed by corporations such as Ichto and H-Brand, which makes them
as valuable as spies as they are as silent killers.

Like other tech-ninja, most grow up in a hidden training camp. The clan
chooses for conversion those with poor physical gifts, often disabled or
handicapped youngsters, who still have the zeal and loyalty it demands. They
spend their early years in computer simulations preparing for life as a
living machine, and are converted at about eighteen. Only the face, the brain
and a few organs remain human. Extra limbs, tails and fire-breathing
apparatus are added only for those who can accept such inhuman changes; most
are built to look as human as possible so they can pass unnoticed at a
distance.

Like the ninja juicers and crazies, ''borgs leave their enclaves mainly for
short missions: a recovery, a kidnapping, an assassination. They are also used
heavily, alongside juicers, in military work, sometimes hired out as elite
mercenaries to kingdoms that buy weapons from H-Brand: sabotage of supply
lines, assassination of commanders, ambushes of armored columns, destruction
of bridges and roads. They have earned a dreaded reputation in these missions,
and even true samurai have learned to respect these silent metal juggernauts.

## GM Notes

The clan pays all living expenses, and the ninja spends most of his life in
hidden camps and headquarters. Beyond the listed kit, the equipment section
describes specialized ninja gear; whether a character starts with any of it is
the GM''s call. The character also starts with 1D6x1000 credits'' worth of black
market salable items.

The Japanese Bionic Conversion rules (printed 96) describe light and heavy
bionics in general; the ninja ''borg''s own figures above take precedence.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ninja-borg');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ninja-borg';

